\tag{fdip}
\title{Finite-group symmetry of Gaussian fields}
\date{2026-10-31}

\p{Which parts of a real field can a graph symmetry keep separate?
The [half-turn sectors](fdip-001A) answer this for one involution.
For a general finite group, the same question leads to orthogonal
projectors indexed by complex characters paired under conjugation.
The prerequisites are [signed endpoint actions](fdip-003B),
[massive graph precision](fdip-000A) and the
[group-algebra extension](fdip-003N).}

\p{Signed symmetries preserve the quadratic energy even when an edge
is reversed. Maschke averaging and the complex central-idempotent
formula supply the representation theory; the real projector theorem
then gives a complete orthogonal decomposition preserved by precision.
The cyclic and dihedral calculations show the resulting subspaces and
eigenvalues explicitly.}

